This product is derived from vCluster
(https://github.com/loft-sh/vcluster), Copyright Loft Labs, Inc. and the
vCluster authors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. vk8s
holds none of vCluster's source files. It is written in Bend after
vCluster's behaviour: its command line and messages, the vcluster.yaml
format, its label, annotation and object names, its chart defaults and
templates (among them the CoreDNS manifests), and its Go tests, which
laws/ and tests/ restate as Bend laws and test cases. The files that do
so name the vCluster file they follow.

The release assets of vk8s hold unchanged third-party programs, each
under its own license: the Linux kernel, BusyBox, Kubernetes, etcd, kine,
konnectivity, containerd, runc, the CNI plugins, gVisor, kube-router,
flannel, CoreDNS, parts of Debian 13, Mozilla's CA certificates and, for
macOS, OpenSSL. THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md lists each with its version, its
license and where its source is.

The vk8s binary links bend-kube-runtime and bend-vmm
(https://github.com/chenhunghan/bend-kube,
https://github.com/chenhunghan/bend-vmm), both MIT.
